<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarnath</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarnath is a site near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varanasi">Varanasi</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, where the Buddha gave his first sermon in the deer park of Isipatana. It became a major monastic centre: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a> raised a pillar there whose lion capital is now India's national emblem, and the Dhamek Stupa dates largely from the Gupta period. The monasteries declined after the 12th century, and the site was excavated from the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarnath.jpg" alt="Sarnath" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yusuke Kawasaki · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Buddhist_monasteries_near_Dhamekh_Stupa_Monument_Site,_Sarnath.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
